questions.prompt:
A B-tree index exists on `(a, b, c)`. Under the classic leftmost-prefix rule, for how many of these WHERE clauses can the index seek on the leading column `a`?

```text
(1) a = 1;
(2) b = 2;
(3) a = 1 AND b = 2;
(4) a = 1 AND c = 3;
(5) b = 2 AND c = 3;
(6) a = 1 AND b = 2 AND c = 3
```

